614
00:23:21,754 --> 00:23:23,556
[keyboard clicks]               

615
00:23:23,623 --> 00:23:25,224
- Captain Garnet,               
   the sun won't come up there  

616
00:23:25,291 --> 00:23:26,426
 for another five hours.        

617
00:23:26,492 --> 00:23:27,693
  The shields will hold         

618
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:29,662
 approximately one hour,        
  three minutes.                

619
00:23:29,729 --> 00:23:31,097
 - Alicia, I'm going to need you

620
00:23:31,164 --> 00:23:33,232
   to figure out a way          
    to make them last longer.   

621
00:23:33,299 --> 00:23:36,035
 - Yeah? Do you not think we've 
 already been trying to do that?

622
00:23:36,102 --> 00:23:37,236
   - We'll keep working on it.  

623
00:23:37,303 --> 00:23:38,704
   - Keep me informed.          

624
00:23:38,771 --> 00:23:40,373
   Garnet out.                  

625
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:41,574
  - All right, come on.         

626
00:23:41,641 --> 00:23:43,743
Come on.                        
 We've got this.                

627
00:23:43,810 --> 00:23:46,312
   I've spent 50 years          
 studying solar storms.         

628
00:23:46,379 --> 00:23:47,980
  I know everything about them. 

629
00:23:48,047 --> 00:23:49,949
 All we have to do is change the
  polarity on the Gravelaxacon, 

630
00:23:50,016 --> 00:23:53,252
  and we can--                  

631
00:23:53,319 --> 00:23:56,322
   Wait. I'm listening to this  
as I'm saying it.               

632
00:23:56,389 --> 00:23:57,957
   It's all garbage, isn't it?  

633
00:23:58,024 --> 00:23:59,392
 - It was a dream, Ian.         

634
00:23:59,459 --> 00:24:01,093
   Anything you think           
   you taught yourself          

635
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:03,696
 was your brain making stuff up.

636
00:24:03,763 --> 00:24:06,265
 - Yeah, right.                 

637
00:24:06,332 --> 00:24:08,668
 It wasn't real.                
 None of it was.                

638
00:24:08,734 --> 00:24:11,037
  - Ian, focus!                 
   We need to figure this out.  

639
00:24:11,103 --> 00:24:12,939
 Otherwise, we're going         
 to have to abandon them        

640
00:24:13,005 --> 00:24:15,208
  to save the rest of the crew. 

641
00:24:15,274 --> 00:24:16,776
   [thud and rumbling]          

642
00:24:16,843 --> 00:24:21,214
- Sharon, we're going to        
   have to make a run for it.   

643
00:24:21,280 --> 00:24:24,784
 - Yeah.                        
   Yeah, you're right.          

644
00:24:24,851 --> 00:24:27,320
   OK, Kimi and I will          
   lay down cover fire          

645
00:24:27,386 --> 00:24:28,721
   to keep the creatures away   

646
00:24:28,788 --> 00:24:30,122
 as you and the doc help        
   the admiral to the shuttle.  

647
00:24:30,189 --> 00:24:31,257
   We can figure out--          

648
00:24:31,324 --> 00:24:33,392
- There's no way                
 to lay down cover fire.        

649
00:24:33,459 --> 00:24:35,061
Bullets don't hurt them.        

650
00:24:35,127 --> 00:24:36,762
   - Then what do you suggest?  

651
00:24:36,829 --> 00:24:38,531
  - Well, we can all leave this 
room during the darkness,       

652
00:24:38,598 --> 00:24:40,266
  and we'll get                 
   shredded to death.           

653
00:24:40,333 --> 00:24:42,635
  Or--                          

654
00:24:42,702 --> 00:24:45,037
[groans]                        

655
00:24:45,104 --> 00:24:47,006
  We can stay in here.          

656
00:24:47,073 --> 00:24:50,409
  And be crushed to death when  
 this building collapses on us. 

657
00:24:50,476 --> 00:24:52,945
 Depends on how you want to die.

658
00:24:53,012 --> 00:24:54,614
   - Bet he's fun at parties.   

