00:31:44,990 --> 00:31:47,092
  We don't want                 
 anyone else sacrificed         

813
00:31:47,159 --> 00:31:48,627
for your mistake                
 in coming here.                

814
00:31:48,694 --> 00:31:52,197
  - Hang on just a sec.         
  - He's right.                 

815
00:31:52,264 --> 00:31:53,799
  Alicia, Ian,                  
   you have to go now.          

816
00:31:53,866 --> 00:31:55,401
 It's too risky for you to stay.
  - No.                         

817
00:31:55,467 --> 00:31:57,102
 No way.                        
   - Ian, listen to me.         

818
00:31:57,169 --> 00:31:59,672
It's OK.                        
  We'll find a way to survive.  

819
00:31:59,738 --> 00:32:01,206
   OK?                          
   You can come back.           

820
00:32:01,273 --> 00:32:03,108
   - Look, no, Sharon!          
 Just--                         

821
00:32:03,175 --> 00:32:04,743
 [sighs]                        
Alicia, come on.                

822
00:32:04,810 --> 00:32:06,779
Just do that genius thing       
  you do and fix this.          

823
00:32:06,845 --> 00:32:08,948
  - I'm sorry,                  
but I'm all out of ideas.       

824
00:32:09,014 --> 00:32:10,916
  [tense music]                 

825
00:32:10,983 --> 00:32:13,252
 - Come on, Ian.                

826
00:32:13,319 --> 00:32:14,653
  Wait.                         

827
00:32:14,720 --> 00:32:16,555
  Wait.                         
 I have an idea.                

828
00:32:16,622 --> 00:32:18,023
 - Did it come from your dream? 

829
00:32:18,090 --> 00:32:20,659
   - Those things down there,   
   they avoid sunlight, right?  

830
00:32:20,726 --> 00:32:21,827
 - Yeah.                        

831
00:32:21,894 --> 00:32:24,163
 - So all we have to do         
is create more sunlight.        

832
00:32:24,229 --> 00:32:25,597
 - How?                         

833
00:32:25,664 --> 00:32:30,269
 - This Ark is equipped         
   with solar sails, isn't it?  

834
00:32:30,336 --> 00:32:32,771
   - Yes, and they're           
   highly reflective.           

835
00:32:32,838 --> 00:32:33,639
  - Reflective.                 

836
00:32:33,706 --> 00:32:35,874
 - Ian, you're a genius!        

837
00:32:35,941 --> 00:32:38,277
   - Come on.                   

838
00:32:38,344 --> 00:32:41,080
   - Captain Garnet, we might   
 be able to use the solar sails 

839
00:32:41,146 --> 00:32:44,316
   to reflect sunlight to the   
  surface, make a path for you. 

840
00:32:44,383 --> 00:32:47,086
  - [chuckles]                  
   Alicia, you little beauty.   

841
00:32:47,152 --> 00:32:49,288
- Do it.                        

842
00:32:49,355 --> 00:32:50,756
- Sasha, move us                
   into higher orbit.           

843
00:32:53,559 --> 00:32:56,328
- Sounds like you've got        
   some smart people, Captain.  

844
00:32:56,395 --> 00:32:58,464
- Grab a helmet.                

845
00:32:58,530 --> 00:33:01,467
  [tense music]                 

846
00:33:01,533 --> 00:33:07,639
   ♪ ♪                          

847
00:33:18,684 --> 00:33:22,087
   [creatures hissing]          

848
00:33:22,154 --> 00:33:23,856
    - OK. Go.                   

849
00:33:23,922 --> 00:33:30,662
   ♪ ♪                          

850
00:33:34,666 --> 00:33:36,869
 [creatures chittering]         

851
00:33:36,935 --> 00:33:43,375
   ♪ ♪                          

852
00:33:45,110 --> 00:33:48,247
  [creatures growling]          

853
00:33:48,313 --> 00:33:51,950
   ♪ ♪                          

854
00:33:52,017 --> 00:33:53,752
 - Run!                         

855
00:33:53,819 --> 00:33:56,388
  - [screaming]                 
 - Doc!                         

856
00:33:56,455 --> 00:33:59,558
  - [screaming]                 

857
00:34:04,029 --> 00:34:05,431
 - Shit!                        

858
00:34:05,497 --> 00:34:06,932
   - Sails are                  
   starting to burn up.         

859
00:34:06,999 --> 00:34:09,935
  Hurry.                        
   - Kimi, keep going!          

860
00:34:10,002 --> 00:34:11,170
  - OK.                         
Let's go.                       

861
00:34:11,236 --> 00:34:14,039
   ♪ ♪                          

862
00:34:14,106 --> 00:34:15,340
  - Any ideas?                  

863
00:34:15,407 --> 00:34:17,242
  - We're going to have         
   to go through the darkness.  

864
00:34:17,309 --> 00:34:18,877
  - Shoot our way out?          

865
00:34:18,944 --> 00:34:20,412
- He said bullets               
don't stop them.                

866
00:34:20,479 --> 00:34:23,449
 - Yeah. Unless you got anything
  else, I think we have to try. 

867
00:34:23,515 --> 00:34:25,050
   - OK. Back-to-back           
  defensive formation.          

868
00:34:25,117 --> 00:34:26,552
 Come on. Get behind me.        

869
00:34:26,618 --> 00:34:29,321
   ♪ ♪                          

870
00:34:29,388 --> 00:34:31,523
- Sharon.                       

871
00:34:31,590 --> 00:34:33,625
It has truly been               
   an honor serving with you.   

872
00:34:33,692 --> 00:34:35,094
   - Likewise, James.           

873
00:34:35,160 --> 00:34:36,929
   But we're going to continue  
  serving together, OK?         

874
00:34:36,995 --> 00:34:39,631
What, it's like,                
 only 25 meters?                

875
00:34:39,698 --> 00:34:41,733
- Listen, if you                
  make it out of this--         

876
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:42,901
- James.                        

877
00:34:42,968 --> 00:34:45,537
  - If you make it out of this  
 and I don't...                 

878
00:34:45,604 --> 00:34:47,339
  you tell Eva I love her, OK?  

879
00:34:47,406 --> 00:34:49,775
 - We're both making it         
out of here, OK?                

880
00:34:49,842 --> 00:34:51,043
   You ready?                   

881
00:34:51,110 --> 00:34:52,111
- Ready.                        

882
00:34:52,177 --> 00:34:53,412
   - On three.                  

883
00:34:53,479 --> 00:34:56,515
One, two, three.                

884
00:34:56,582 --> 00:34:59,718
[both screaming]                

885
00:35:07,493 --> 00:35:08,961
 Brice, come on.                
  We're close.                  

886
00:35:09,027 --> 00:35:11,497
 Come on, Brice!                

887
00:35:11,563 --> 00:35:12,631
   - Come on.                   

888
00:35:12,698 --> 00:35:14,399
  Yes!                          
 - Yes!                         

889
00:35:14,466 --> 00:35:15,767
   Come on, let's get           
 to the shuttle.                

890
00:35:15,834 --> 00:35:16,602
- Uh-huh.                       

891
00:35:16,668 --> 00:35:22,608
   ♪ ♪                          

892
00:35:25,244 --> 00:35:26,778
  Shit.                         

893
00:35:26,845 --> 00:35:28,780
   - Keep going. Back-to-back.  
Come on.                        

894
00:35:28,847 --> 00:35:31,950
 [soft suspenseful music]       

895
00:35:32,017 --> 00:35:34,186
   ♪ ♪                          

896
00:35:34,253 --> 00:35:37,156
[chittering and growling]       

897
00:35:37,222 --> 00:35:38,857
   ♪ ♪                          

898
00:35:38,924 --> 00:35:43,128
  - [shouting]                  
  - [shouting]                  

899
00:35:47,866 --> 00:35:49,434
  - Can you get to the shuttle? 

900
00:35:49,501 --> 00:35:50,669
I'm going to pull               
   them off this way.           

901
00:35:50,736 --> 00:35:52,037
  - No!                         
 Stay together!                 

902
00:35:52,104 --> 00:35:55,007
  - [shouting]                  
  Follow me, you ugly bastard!  

903
00:35:55,073 --> 00:35:58,076
   ♪ ♪                          

904
00:35:58,143 --> 00:35:59,344
[groans]                        

905
00:35:59,411 --> 00:36:01,180
- Brice!                        

906
00:36:01,246 --> 00:36:04,183
  - [groaning]                  

907
00:36:04,249 --> 00:36:07,219
   ♪ ♪                          

908
00:36:07,286 --> 00:36:10,055
   [screaming]                  

909
00:36:10,122 --> 00:36:12,224
 - Go prep the shuttle.         

910
00:36:12,291 --> 00:36:16,028
 [somber dramatic music]        

911
00:36:16,094 --> 00:36:17,329
- No, no.                       

912
00:36:17,396 --> 00:36:18,864
   ♪ ♪                          

913
00:36:18,931 --> 00:36:20,032
 - Run!                         

914
00:36:20,098 --> 00:36:23,235
[groans]                        

915
00:36:23,302 --> 00:36:25,971
   - Captain!                   
  Run!                          

916
00:36:26,038 --> 00:36:27,005
- [yelps]                       

917
00:36:27,072 --> 00:36:32,511
   ♪ ♪                          

918
00:36:32,578 --> 00:36:33,879
   - Come on, Captain.          

919
00:36:33,946 --> 00:36:36,381
Captain,                        
 we have to keep moving.        

920
00:36:36,448 --> 00:36:37,649
- Brice!                        

921
00:36:37,716 --> 00:36:39,251
  - Come one, Captain!          
 We have to go!                 

922
00:36:39,318 --> 00:36:40,652
Come on, Captain!               
Come on!                        

923
00:36:40,719 --> 00:36:42,487
- No! No!                       
 - Now!                         

924
00:36:42,554 --> 00:36:49,695
   ♪ ♪                          

925
00:36:51,296 --> 00:36:54,233
   - [panting]                  

926
00:36:54,299 --> 00:37:01,240
   ♪ ♪                          

927
00:37:06,311 --> 00:37:08,614
   - Brace for launch.          

928
00:37:08,680 --> 00:37:11,783
   [engines rumbling]           

929
00:37:16,555 --> 00:37:16,588
   -                            

930
00:37:16,588 --> 00:37:16,622
   - [p                         

931
00:37:16,622 --> 00:37:16,655
   - [pan                       

932
00:37:16,655 --> 00:37:16,688
   - [panti                     

933
00:37:16,688 --> 00:37:16,722
   - [panting                   

934
00:37:16,722 --> 00:37:19,291
   - [panting]                  

935
00:37:22,794 --> 00:37:25,097
  [somber music]                

936
00:37:25,163 --> 00:37:28,567
   - Are you injured?           

937
00:37:28,634 --> 00:37:29,801
  - No.                         

938
00:37:29,868 --> 00:37:33,905
   ♪ ♪                          

939
00:37:33,972 --> 00:37:36,842
[crying]                        

940
00:37:36,908 --> 00:37:44,049
   ♪ ♪                          

941
00:37:50,122 --> 00:37:52,224
 - Hey.                         

942
00:37:52,291 --> 00:37:53,625
  I'm starving.                 

943
00:37:53,692 --> 00:37:56,495
 Uh, do you have any of         
  those, um, mushroom burgers?  

944
00:37:56,561 --> 00:37:57,562
  - Yeah, sure.                 

945
00:37:57,629 --> 00:38:00,299
  - Oh, and a--                 
   a vodka with soda.           

946
00:38:10,676 --> 00:38:12,244
 Thanks.                        

947
00:38:12,311 --> 00:38:19,318
   ♪ ♪                          

948
00:38:20,752 --> 00:38:23,288
 [sighs]                        

949
00:38:23,355 --> 00:38:25,190
 Can I join you?                

950
00:38:27,025 --> 00:38:29,194
 - You shouldn't feel obligated.

951
00:38:29,261 --> 00:38:31,163
 - What does that mean?         

952
00:38:31,229 --> 00:38:32,931
 - I know how much you hate me. 

953
00:38:32,998 --> 00:38:34,232
   - I don't hate you.          

954
00:38:34,299 --> 00:38:35,467
   Don't get me wrong.          

955
00:38:35,534 --> 00:38:38,470
I did hate you, but a lot       
has happened since then.        

956
00:38:38,537 --> 00:38:41,573
  Uh, I have to go out          
 in the exploration zone        

957
00:38:41,640 --> 00:38:44,976
   to finish collecting plant   
   samples in the underbrush.   

958
00:38:45,043 --> 00:38:46,611
 [soft suspenseful music]       

959
00:38:46,678 --> 00:38:48,347
You want to come?               

960
00:38:50,482 --> 00:38:51,983
- I don't need your pity,       
 Angus.                         

961
00:38:52,050 --> 00:38:53,518
I'm fine.                       
   - Nothing to do with pity.   

962
00:38:53,585 --> 00:38:54,486
I swear.                        

963
00:38:54,553 --> 00:38:55,821
   Gabby's too afraid           
to go out there,                

964
00:38:55,887 --> 00:38:59,458
   but I'd feel safer           
  if you came instead.          

965
00:38:59,524 --> 00:39:02,627
You know,                       
   with your implants and all.  

966
00:39:02,694 --> 00:39:06,465
   ♪ ♪                          

967
00:39:06,531 --> 00:39:07,933
 - Can I finish                 
   my sandwich first?           

968
00:39:07,999 --> 00:39:12,471
   ♪ ♪                          

969
00:39:12,537 --> 00:39:13,872
    [computer chimes]           
  - James, you're late.         

970
00:39:13,939 --> 00:39:16,942
  I almost changed back into--  

971
00:39:17,008 --> 00:39:18,343
   oh.                          

972
00:39:22,981 --> 00:39:24,316
 Captain Garnet?                

973
00:39:24,383 --> 00:39:26,351
   - Eva, um--                  

974
00:39:26,418 --> 00:39:29,354
   [soft somber music]          

975
00:39:29,421 --> 00:39:30,922
    I really wanted to          
    do this in person,          

976
00:39:30,989 --> 00:39:32,991
   but I know you guys          
 have your regular calls,       

977
00:39:33,058 --> 00:39:35,394
  so I thought I shouldn't wait.

978
00:39:35,460 --> 00:39:39,998
 - Just tell me, please.        

979
00:39:40,065 --> 00:39:41,533
  - OK.                         

980
00:39:43,802 --> 00:39:47,105
   When we were making a run to 
   the shuttle to escape Ross,  

981
00:39:47,172 --> 00:39:50,308
    James was attacked by some  

982
00:39:50,375 --> 00:39:52,110
  indigenous creatures,         
 really big ones.               

983
00:39:52,177 --> 00:39:54,479
   And--[sobs]                  

984
00:39:54,546 --> 00:39:57,048
    I'm so sorry, Eva,          
  but he's dead.                

985
00:39:57,115 --> 00:40:01,019
   - [crying]                   

986
00:40:01,086 --> 00:40:02,220
  Are you sure?                 

987
00:40:02,287 --> 00:40:05,524
   ♪ ♪                          

988
00:40:05,590 --> 00:40:09,294
  - And I wish--                
   oh, I wish I wasn't.         

989
00:40:09,361 --> 00:40:13,498
    But I saw him die myself.   

990
00:40:13,565 --> 00:40:17,702
    I'm so sorry, Eva.          

991
00:40:17,769 --> 00:40:20,005
   ♪ ♪                          

992
00:40:20,071 --> 00:40:21,840
   Right before                 
  we made a run for it,         

993
00:40:21,907 --> 00:40:26,745
    Brice told me to tell you   
  he loves you so much.         

994
00:40:26,812 --> 00:40:29,147
 You know he did.               

995
00:40:29,214 --> 00:40:30,715
- [sobs]                        

996
00:40:30,782 --> 00:40:36,555
   ♪ ♪                          

997
00:40:36,621 --> 00:40:38,323
 [sighs]                        

998
00:40:38,390 --> 00:40:40,692
   Please send me the WD logs   

999
00:40:40,759 --> 00:40:43,662
and the hull camera files       
  from the shuttle and the Ark. 

1000
00:40:43,728 --> 00:40:47,799
 - Eva, you don't               
 want to see it.                

1001
00:40:47,866 --> 00:40:50,735
 It's pretty bad.               

1002
00:40:50,802 --> 00:40:54,873
 - Seeing it myself is the only 
 way I'll be able to accept it. 

1003
00:40:54,940 --> 00:40:58,343
   ♪ ♪                          

1004
00:40:58,410 --> 00:41:00,645
 - So how do you                
like being free?                

1005
00:41:00,712 --> 00:41:02,981
 - I didn't really mind         
being locked up.                

1006
00:41:03,048 --> 00:41:05,650
  At least no one bothered me.  

1007
00:41:05,717 --> 00:41:09,087
   [rustling]                   

1008
00:41:09,154 --> 00:41:12,057
   [suspenseful music]          

1009
00:41:12,123 --> 00:41:13,825
   ♪ ♪                          

1010
00:41:13,892 --> 00:41:16,628
 - Where are you going?         
Kelly, come back.               

1011
00:41:16,695 --> 00:41:18,163
 - Did you hear that over there?

1012
00:41:18,230 --> 00:41:20,432
  - Yes, which is why we should 
 be going the other way.        

1013
00:41:20,499 --> 00:41:21,500
- Don't you want                
   to know what it is?          

1014
00:41:21,566 --> 00:41:23,468
  - No!                         
Not particularly.               

1015
00:41:23,535 --> 00:41:25,971
- Come on, Angus.               
   That's why you brought me.   

1016
00:41:27,472 --> 00:41:29,274
   - [groans]                   

1017
00:41:29,341 --> 00:41:32,444
  [rumbling, whooshing]         

1018
00:41:34,613 --> 00:41:37,716
   [suspenseful music]          

1019
00:41:37,782 --> 00:41:44,723
   ♪ ♪                          

